James inquired whether to hold a public event at the UNFCCC COP during the first or second week to maximize engagement and impact. I explained that the first week focuses on technical negotiations, making it suitable for engaging experts. In contrast, the second week attracts higher-profile attendees like ministers and heads of state, resulting in increased media attention. I advised that the second week generally offers better opportunities for broader engagement, especially if the event aligns with key themes or announcements. However, I emphasized the importance of securing an optimal time slot due to the packed schedule.
